.TH LFILTER 1 "2026-05" "BusyPipe 1.0" "BusyPipe Manual"
.SH NAME
lfilter \- CSV stream filter and field projector for BusyPipe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lfilter
[\fB\-\-where\fR \fIexpr\fR]
[\fB\-\-contains\fR \fIfield=substring\fR]
[\fB\-\-select\fR \fIf1,f2,...\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fBcsv\fR|\fBjson\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lfilter
reads a CSV stream from standard input (first line treated as header),
applies optional filter conditions and field projection, and writes the
filtered result to standard output.

It is the second stage of the BusyPipe ETL pipeline:

.nf
  lparser | lfilter | lstore
.fi

Multiple filters (e.g.\& \fB\-\-where\fR and \fB\-\-contains\fR) are combined with
logical AND.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-where " " \fI"field<op>value"\fR
Numeric or lexicographic comparison filter.
Supported operators: \fB==  !=  >  >=  <  <=\fR.
If both sides look like numbers, numeric comparison is used;
otherwise lexicographic.
.TP
.BR \-\-contains " " \fI"field=substring"\fR
Keep only rows where the specified field contains the given substring.
.TP
.BR \-\-select " " \fI"f1,f2,..."\fR
Output only the listed fields (column projection).
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fBcsv\fR|\fBjson\fR
Output format.
\fBcsv\fR (default) writes CSV with a header row.
\fBjson\fR writes JSONL — one JSON object per row.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (zero or more rows matched).
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, unknown field name, or invalid expression.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Filter by numeric status code
.nf
  lfilter \-\-where 'status>=400'
.fi
.SS Project selected fields
.nf
  lfilter \-\-where 'status>=400' \-\-select 'ip,path,status'
.fi
.SS Substring filter with JSON output
.nf
  lfilter \-\-contains 'user=admin' \-\-format json
.fi
.SS Full pipeline
.nf
  lparser \-\-format nginx \-\-csv < access.log \\
    | lfilter \-\-where 'status>=400' \-\-select 'ip,path,status' \\
    | lstore  \-\-db errors.tsv \-\-put \-\-key\-field ip \-\-ttl 3600
.fi
.SH COMPATIBILITY
Implements a subset of \fBawk\fR(1) filtering and \fBcut\fR(1) field selection.
The comparison semantics follow GNU \fBawk\fR numeric-string rules.
.SH BUGS
Only one \fB\-\-where\fR expression is supported per invocation.
Quoted CSV fields (containing commas) are not yet handled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lparser (1),
.BR lstore (1),
.BR cut (1),
.BR awk (1)
